# evidence-cmd: cd plugins/webster && echo '--- FR-012 / FR-017 / GI-003: the contract `types` prints, per reader ---'; python3 scripts/doctype.py types | sed -n '/^Audiences/,/^ISO/p'; echo '--- every kind check_lens can report, and the reader gate over each ---'; awk '/^    named = \[\]/,/^    seen = set\(\)/' scripts/doctype.py | grep -E 'if audience == "user"|\.finditer\(|named\.append\('
# evidence-for: US-003, FR-012, FR-017, AC-014
#
# FR-012 / FR-017. `doctype.py types` is where a writer reads the lens before
# the lens reads them, so a class missing from it is a writer told a thing is
# allowed by the same build that defects it.
#
# The second block is the whole of check_lens's collection loop, filtered to
# the five kinds it can append and the audience conditions over them, with the
# indentation left in because the indentation is the gate. An internal symbol
# name and part of the architecture are collected for whatever reader
# LENS_MAY_NOT names a contract for; an environment variable, a request route
# and a command-line flag are each reached only when the audience is `user`.
#
# Read against the contract above: the user line names all five, the operator
# line names the two that fire for an operator and none of the three that do
# not, and the developer line -- which has no contract to keep -- names none.
# The guard for this read two of the five before D-093, and the index sentence
# over it claimed every class.
--- FR-012 / FR-017 / GI-003: the contract `types` prints, per reader ---
Audiences. The audience is a lens first and a reading grade second:
  user       grade 10  Uses the product. No development, sysadmin or DevOps background.
             assumes general computer literacy and a real reason to be here
             may not name internal symbols, any route path, command-line flags, environment variables and architecture
  operator   grade 13  Installs, configures and runs the product. Comfortable with a terminal.
             assumes a terminal, a package manager, environment variables, a hosting dashboard
             may not name internal symbols and architecture
  developer  grade 15  Builds against the product or contributes to it.
             assumes the language, the toolchain, and how to read source
             may name anything in the system

ISO/IEC/IEEE 26514 quality characteristics:
--- every kind check_lens can report, and the reader gate over each ---
        for m in CODE_IDENT.finditer(line):
                named.append((n, f"`{m.group(1)}`", "an internal symbol name"))
        for m in ENV_VAR.finditer(line):
            if audience == "user" and m.group(1) in env_vars:
                named.append((n, f"`{m.group(1)}`", "an environment variable"))
        if audience == "user":
            for m in ROUTE_PATH.finditer(line):
                named.append((n, m.group(1) or m.group(2), "a request route"))
            for m in FLAG.finditer(line):
                named.append((n, f"`{m.group(1)}`", "a command-line flag"))
        for m in ARCH_HARD.finditer(line):
            named.append((n, m.group(1), "part of the architecture"))
